                <pb facs="0463" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg367"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure in No. 383.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Extract from a telegram from Governor Sir F. Cardew to
                        Mr. Chamberlain.</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Regret to inform you that the following American missionaries, Mr. and Mrs. Cain,
                    Misses Archer, Hatfield, and Schenck, killed by insurgent bands at Rotifunk; but
                    Miss Ward, as well as the following American missionaries, Mr. and Mrs.
                    Minshall, from Shengeh, and Miss Mullen, from Mamaligi, are here quite safe.
                    Please inform American ambassador.</p>
            </div>
